                                "target_word": "voracious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                        "entry_id": "69f7db48-7d3e-349d-81e7-6386fa7d20c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wanting or devouring great quantities of food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person or their appetite"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18785019-ce9d-4c0f-9f34-477568beca09",
                                                "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                                "text": "He is voracious by suppertime."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faca3946-9b05-460a-8369-0b0dee6be41a",
                                                "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                                "text": "His appetite is voracious by suppertime."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26bb467f-a0ba-488b-a2f9-214ea753691c",
                                                "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                                "text": "I never had so much as […] one wish to God to direct me whither I should go, or to keep me from the danger which apparently surrounded me, as well from voracious creatures as cruel savages."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "390a1467-bacb-4dc7-80be-887c63820aad",
                                                "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                                "text": "The old man was up, betimes, next morning, and waited impatiently for the appearance of his new associate, who after a delay that seemed interminable, at length presented himself, and commenced a voracious assault on the breakfast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abda9c59-7398-4a96-8229-b45d9e5a03a2",
                                                "sense_id": "2145405c-02cc-3960-9285-e8bb33d6992c",
                                                "text": "Retreating before stronger breeds, hungry and voracious, the Eskimo has drifted to the inhospitable polar regions, the Pygmy to the fever-rotten jungles of Africa."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66bd87c4-e025-32b2-ad80-293c956af1e0",
                                        "entry_id": "69f7db48-7d3e-349d-81e7-6386fa7d20c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a great appetite for anything; eager."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16ad4c53-d970-4d87-b0ab-d87420c4875b",
                                                "sense_id": "66bd87c4-e025-32b2-ad80-293c956af1e0",
                                                "text": "a voracious reader"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0baeadcf-f67d-4d11-97e6-2b77fca5aebd",
                                                "sense_id": "66bd87c4-e025-32b2-ad80-293c956af1e0",
                                                "text": "If he carried chiefly his appetite, a zeal for tiled bathrooms, a conviction that the Pullman car is the acme of human comfort, and a belief that it is proper to tip waiters, taxicab drivers, and barbers, but under no circumstances station agents and ushers, then his Odyssey will be replete with good meals and bad meals, bathing adventures, compartment-train escapades, and voracious demands for money."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5f6cbd8-975d-4de0-9f2c-d800cd929b62",
                                                "sense_id": "66bd87c4-e025-32b2-ad80-293c956af1e0",
                                                "text": "Methodical and voracious, these hackers wanted all the files they could find."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6487ca0-b871-4d37-b032-6c8f89f67f16",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3c19b1c-24de-3db7-bd89-d8e636d68e45",
                        "source_sense_id": "b3df5aab-4783-3036-83e9-233420c3030b",
                        "target_lang_word": "gluttonous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gluttonous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd5e1bda-0a9f-3665-aa30-cf69a443eb62",
                                        "entry_id": "f4754f6a-61bc-3c56-b935-652eee7755f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Given to excessive eating; prone to overeating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e030d88-0d8f-4f01-a463-8c4ee7ad6a32",
                                                "sense_id": "fd5e1bda-0a9f-3665-aa30-cf69a443eb62",
                                                "text": "Behold a man gluttonous, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                        "entry_id": "f4754f6a-61bc-3c56-b935-652eee7755f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Greedy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58e44b65-d415-4ea3-8a50-5b0532bec79a",
                                                "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                                "text": "Then they could smile and fawn upon his debts, / And take down the interest into their gluttonous maws."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "783f940f-e317-49c8-a507-a66f8ef29523",
                                                "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                                "text": "[\"]The voracious caterpillar when transformed into a butterfly,\" … \"and the gluttonous maggot when become a fly,\" content themselves with a drop or two of honey or some other sweet liquid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e61c196-5445-4407-8e28-591336efe972",
                                                "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                                "text": "Do the feasters gluttonous feast? / Do the corpulent sleepers sleep? have they lock'd and bolted doors? / Still be ours the diet hard, and the blanket on the ground, / Pioneers! O pioneers!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "030a7e03-e48a-4c31-aa67-779aee7ae1fd",
                                                "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                                "text": "Look your last on your dearest ones, / Brothers and husbands, fathers, sons: / Swift they go to the ravenous guns, / The gluttonous guns of War."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9dbcb18-a693-4233-aea7-80c2f0ffe561",
                                                "sense_id": "422ae444-3890-3520-a4de-b18cc536656e",
                                                "text": "One day the mail-man found no village there, / Nor were its folk or houses seen again; / People came out from Aylesbury to stare – / Yet they all told the mail-man it was plain / That he was mad for saying he had spied / The great hill's gluttonous eyes, and jaws stretched wide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5ac31e35-4645-409a-ad74-a6fb8919c22a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3c19b1c-24de-3db7-bd89-d8e636d68e45",
                        "source_sense_id": "b3df5aab-4783-3036-83e9-233420c3030b",
